The code includes a simple mechanism to verify the integrity of the allocated memory at regular intervals by filling the structure with appropriate values, and it provides options to control the frequency and retention period of logs using customizable backoff values. It also handles potential race conditions in a multi-threaded environment by using `pthread_mutex_lock()` and `pthread_mutex_unlock()` when logging allocations.']

