Error handling for memory allocation failures is implemented using standard C functions such as malloc() and realloc().

The code uses a mutex lock to ensure thread-safe access to the buffer when multiple threads are in use. Timestamp generation is not prioritized between speed and accuracy, but you can easily modify the time_t variable within the structure to suit your specific needs.']

