Regarding hashing algorithms, we used a simple 64-bit hash function (`uint64_t hash = prng()`) for our implementation as it offers a good balance between lookup speed and memory usage without excessive collisions. If needed, you can explore other hashing algorithms such as FNV1a or MurmurHash to further optimize the hash table performance.

